---
layout: tool.njk
eleventyComputed:
  title: "SEO Scorecard — SEO Toolkit"
  description: "Get a comprehensive SEO score for your page. Check title, meta description, headings, images, links, and more against best practices."
  canonical: "/tools/seo-scorecard/"
  tool:
    slug: "seo-scorecard"
    title: "SEO Scorecard"
    icon: "✅"
    description: "Get a comprehensive SEO score for your page HTML."
  toolScript: "/assets/tools/seo-scorecard/script.js"
---

<section class="tool-area">
  <div class="tool-container">
    <div class="form-group">
      <label for="ss-page-url">Page URL</label>
      <input type="url" id="ss-page-url" placeholder="https://example.com/your-page">
      <p class="form-hint">Used for display purposes and canonical URL checks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="form-group">
      <label for="ss-html">Page HTML Source *</label>
      <textarea id="ss-html" rows="14" placeholder="Paste the full HTML source of your page here (Ctrl+U to view source in most browsers)..."></textarea>
      <p class="form-hint">Paste the complete HTML source for the most accurate analysis.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-actions">
      <button class="btn-primary" onclick="runScorecard()">Run SEO Audit</button>
      <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="clearScorecard()">Clear</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="tool-output" id="ss-result">
    <h3>SEO Scorecard</h3>
    <div id="ss-score-ring"></div>
    <div id="ss-categories"></div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:20px">Detailed Checks</h4>
    <div id="ss-checks"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <details>
    <summary>What does an SEO scorecard measure?</summary>
    <p>An SEO scorecard evaluates your page against established on-page SEO best practices: title tag quality, meta description, heading structure, image alt attributes, internal/external links, page size, and structured data presence. It covers the technical foundations that search engines use to understand your content.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Is a high SEO score guaranteed to improve rankings?</summary>
    <p>No. On-page SEO is just one factor among hundreds. Content quality, backlinks, user experience, and domain authority are equally important. However, fixing on-page issues removes technical barriers that prevent search engines from properly crawling and understanding your content.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>How often should I run an SEO audit?</summary>
    <p>Run audits after significant content changes, page redesigns, or as part of a monthly SEO maintenance routine. For high-traffic pages, monthly audits are recommended. For blog posts, auditing before and after major edits is sufficient.</p>
  </details>
</section>

<style>
#ss-score-ring {
  text-align: center;
  margin: 20px 0;
}
.score-circle {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 140px;
  height: 140px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  line-height: 140px;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 2.5em;
  font-weight: 800;
  border: 8px solid;
}
.score-circle .label { display: block; font-size: 0.35em; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 4px; }
#ss-categories {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
  margin: 16px 0;
}
.ss-cat {
  background: var(--card-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 14px;
}
.ss-cat .cat-name { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
.ss-cat .cat-score { font-size: 1.3em; font-weight: 700; }
.ss-cat .cat-bar { height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--border); margin-top: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
.ss-cat .cat-bar-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 3px; transition: width 0.4s; }
.ss-check {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 10px;
  padding: 10px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  font-size: 0.9em;
}
.ss-check .icon { font-size: 1.2em; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
.ss-check.pass .icon { color: var(--success); }
.ss-check.fail .icon { color: var(--error); }
.ss-check.warn .icon { color: var(--warning); }
</style>

<script>
function clearScorecard() {
  document.getElementById("ss-html").value = "";
  document.getElementById("ss-page-url").value = "";
  document.getElementById("ss-score-ring").innerHTML = "";
  document.getElementById("ss-categories").innerHTML = "";
  document.getElementById("ss-checks").innerHTML = "";
}
</script>
